<title>NEW ZEALAND: POLL-Survey of New Zealand Labour Cost data.</title>
<headline>POLL-Survey of New Zealand Labour Cost data.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Labour Cost Index data for the June 1997 quarter are due on Friday August 22 at 10.45 a.m. (2245 GMT).</p>
<p>INDICATOR		     PERIOD	    AVG F/CAST    PREVIOUS</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>A. Salary &amp; wage rates</p>
<p>including overtime	  June 1997 qtr     +0.66 pct   +0.7 pct</p>
<p>B. Salary &amp; wage rates</p>
<p>incl. overtime		From Jun 96 qtr   +2.57 pct   +2.2 pct</p>
<p>C. Salary &amp; ordinary time</p>
<p>wage rates		    From Jun 96 qtr   +1.88 pct   +2.2 pct</p>
<p>D. Overtime wage rates    From Jun 96 qtr    +1.8 pct   +1.9 pct</p>
<p>E. Private sector</p>
<p>salary &amp; wage rates	 From Jun 96 qtr   +2.24 pct   +2.0 pct</p>
<p>F. Public sector</p>
<p>salary &amp; wage rates	 From Jun 96 qtr   +3.37 pct   +2.9 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Further information:</p>
<p>    FORECAST  RESPONDENTS  MEDIAN	 RANGE</p>
<p>    A	   Seven	  0.6 pct	0.4 to 0.9 pct</p>
<p>    B	   Seven	  2.5 pct	2.4 to 2.8 pct</p>
<p>    C	   Nine	   2.4 pct	0.4 to 2.8 pct</p>
<p>    D	   Five	   2.0 pct	0.3 to 2.5 pct</p>
<p>    E	   Seven	  2.2 pct	2.0 to 2.7 pct</p>
<p>    F	   Six	    3.4 pct	3.1 to 3.7 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Respondents to the survey were: ANZ Investment Bank, ASB Bank, Bankers Trust New Zealand, Bank of New Zealand, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Doyle Paterson Brown, National Bank of New Zealand, SBC Warburg, WestpacTrust.</p>
